The startSession server command has the following format: interface StartSessionCommand { startSession: 1; $clusterTime?: ClusterTime;
} The $clusterTime field should only be sent when gossipping the cluster time. See the section "Gossipping the cluster time" for information on $clusterTime. The startSession command MUST be sent to the admin database. The server response has the following format: interface StartSessionResponse { ok: 1; id: BsonDocument;
} In case of an error, the server response has the following format: interface StartSessionError { ok: 0; errmsg: string; code: number;
} When connected to a replica set the startSession command MUST be sent to the primary if the primary is available. The startSession command MAY be sent to a secondary if there is no primary available at the time the startSession command needs to be run. Drivers SHOULD generate session IDs locally if possible instead of running the startSession command, since running the command requires a network round trip.

